rca of the issue:
Reproduction: (1) LM POST /functions/v1/send-invitation → returns signinCode; (2) UI /first-signin submit → redeem-invite-code returns passwordAlreadySet:false; (3) supabase.auth.verifyOtp({token_hash, type:'magiclink'}) succeeds → session state changes in useAuthStore; (4) FirstSigninScreen calls router.replace('/set-password?projectId=...'); (5) SIMULTANEOUSLY the AuthGuard useEffect fires with (session, inAuthGroup=true) and calls router.replace(getDefaultTabRoute(role)) → wins the race → user lands on /home. Observed: page URL after submit was https://.../home with dashboard for the freshly-created investor. Mitigation: allow /set-password inside the (auth) group for signed-in users. Minimal diff:

```tsx
if (session && inAuthGroup && segments[1] !== 'set-password') {
  router.replace(getDefaultTabRoute(role));
}
```

OR track a `mustSetPassword` flag in useAuthStore set from redeemInviteCode result before verifyOtp, and gate the guard on it.
